//? Title: Rotating calipers: exact support-area order and actual antipodal pairs
//? Subtitle: Actual canonical histories, retained original fixtures and explicit controls
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
Given planar points, find the two with greatest Euclidean separation. The
farthest pair lies on the convex hull. The native implementation now performs a
genuine forward rotating-antipode walk rather than the old exhaustive hull-pair
scan. Actual area and pair events explain the original hand square and seeded
Gaussian cloud.
)

\toc

> Mechanism and mathematical scope

For a CCW hull edge (p_i,p_{i+1}), advance its opposite support point while the
oriented triangle area increases. The support pointer moves forward as the edge
rotates, giving O(H) total area/pair tests after hull construction. Equal-area
ties require testing both opposite endpoints. The native area ordering compares
the exact sign of cross(p_{i+1}-p_i,p_{j+1}-p_i)-cross(p_{i+1}-p_i,p_j-p_i),
using the shared exact dyadic predicate rather than subtracting rounded cross
products. Euclidean candidate distances use widened hypot and finite double
outputs. Hull preparation costs O(N log N); the actual antipode walk is O(H).
Equal represented distances keep the first encountered pair.

> A tiny actual producing history

The table and native concept diagram read the same producing execution. Every
block below is a complete editable C++ program.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/rotating_calipers_tiny.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
#include <filesystem>
#include <print>
#include <algorithm>
#include <cmath>
#include <limits>
#include <numeric>
#include <numbers>
#include <random>
#include <string>
#include <vector>
#include <map>
#include <set>
#include <array>
#include <tuple>
#include <bit>
#include <datamunge/geometry/rotating_calipers.hpp>
int main() {
    namespace a = dm::algorithms;
    namespace g = dm::graphics;
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
    namespace z = dm::geometry;
    auto t = z::polygon_diameter_trace({{0, 0}, {3, 0}, {3, 4}, {0, 4}});
    std::print("| actual event kind | first hull id | second hull id | proposed next | exact area sign | " "actual distance | improved |\n| ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | --- |\n");
    for (const auto &e : t.events)
        std::print("| {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {} |\n", int(e.kind),
                   e.first, e.second, e.next, e.area_sign, e.distance,
                   e.improved);
    g::Diagram d(48, 1100);
    d.node("n0", {0, 0}, std::format("Actual hull vertices {}", t.hull.size()));
    d.node("n1", {5, 0},
           std::format("Actual pointer advances {}", t.pointer_advances));
    d.node("n2", {10, 0},
           std::format("Actual winning distance {}", t.result.distance));
    d.edge("n0", "n1").edge("n1", "n2");
    d.save_svg("build/rotating_calipers_tiny.svg");
}
```
