> API and interpretation

Area-order decisions use the exact canonical predicate for represented finite
coordinates. Distance outputs remain finite double approximations, and equal
represented distances can choose a different equally far pair from the old
exhaustive scan. Selected work excludes sorting, hull construction and
exact-predicate internal word operations. The equal-geometry plotting limits and
square plot area keep x/y distances comparable.

Reusable producers, fixtures and histories live in the canonical C++ library.
Captured records own their values and do not come from a separate report replay.
Selected counters and record/scalar policies are specified at their API
boundaries; they are not peak-byte or wall-time budgets. Synthetic structural
inputs are controlled fixtures for these mechanisms.

> References

- [Toussaint, Solving geometric problems with the rotating calipers (1983)|https://www-cgrl.cs.mcgill.ca/~godfried/publications/calipers.pdf]

